{"id":"CVE-2010-0928","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2010-03-05T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T01:06:52.376Z","description":"OpenSSL 0.9.8i on the Gaisler Research LEON3 SoC on the Xilinx Virtex-II Pro FPGA uses a Fixed Width Exponentiation (FWE) algorithm for certain signature calculations, and does not verify the signature before providing it to a caller, which makes it easier for physically proximate attackers to determine the private key via a modified supply voltage for the microprocessor, related to a \"fault-based attack.\"","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/56750","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"openssl-fwe-weak-security(56750)"},{"url":"http://www.theregister.co.uk/2010/03/04/severe_openssl_vulnerability/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/62808","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"62808"},{"url":"http://rdist.root.org/2010/03/08/attacking-rsa-exponentiation-with-fault-injection/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.eecs.umich.edu/~valeria/research/publications/DATE10RSA.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.networkworld.com/news/2010/030410-rsa-security-attack.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-1378","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"apple","published":"2010-11-15T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T20:16:58.322Z","description":"OpenSSL in Apple Mac OS X 10.6.x before 10.6.5 does not properly perform arithmetic, which allows remote attackers to bypass X.509 certificate authentication via an arbitrary certificate issued by a legitimate Certification Authority.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://support.apple.com/kb/HT4435","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/security-announce/2010//Nov/msg00000.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2010-11-10-1"}],"vendors":["apple","openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-1633","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2010-06-03T14:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T01:28:42.110Z","description":"RSA verification recovery in the EVP_PKEY_verify_recover function in OpenSSL 1.x before 1.0.0a, as used by pkeyutl and possibly other applications, returns uninitialized memory upon failure, which might allow context-dependent attackers to bypass intended key requirements or obtain sensitive information via unspecified vectors.  NOTE: some of these details are obtained from third party information.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2010/1313","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2010-1313"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/40024","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"40024"},{"url":"http://www-01.ibm.com/support/docview.wss?uid=ssg1S1004564","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://cvs.openssl.org/filediff?f=openssl/crypto/rsa/rsa_pmeth.c&v1=1.34&v2=1.34.2.1","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/57353","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"57353"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=598732","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/40503","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"40503"},{"url":"http://cvs.openssl.org/chngview?cn=19693","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.openssl.org/news/secadv_20100601.txt","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-2450","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2019-11-07T20:06:05.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T02:32:16.662Z","description":"The keygen.sh script in Shibboleth SP 2.0 (located in /usr/local/etc/shibboleth by default) uses OpenSSL to create a DES private key which is placed in sp-key.pm. It relies on the root umask (default 22) instead of chmoding the resulting file itself, so the generated private key is world readable by default.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2010-2450","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=571631","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://todos.internet2.edu/browse/SSPCPP-106","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2010-2939","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2010-08-17T17:31:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T02:55:45.367Z","description":"Double free vulnerability in the ssl3_get_key_exchange function in the OpenSSL client (ssl/s3_clnt.c) in OpenSSL 1.0.0a, 0.9.8, 0.9.7, and possibly other versions, when using ECDH, allows context-dependent attackers to cause a denial of service (crash) and possibly execute arbitrary code via a crafted private key with an invalid prime.  NOTE: some sources refer to this as a use-after-free issue.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://slackware.com/security/viewer.php?l=slackware-security&y=2010&m=slackware-security.668793","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SLACKWARE"],"name":"SSA:2010-326-01"},{"url":"http://www.mail-archive.com/openssl-dev%40openssl.org/msg28049.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[openssl-dev] 20100808 Re: openssl-1.0.0a and glibc detected sthg ;)"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=130331363227777&w=2","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"HPSBMA02662"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/42413","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"42413"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/40906","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"40906"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2010/dsa-2100","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-2100"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2010/08/11/6","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20100812 Re: CVE Request: openssl double free"},{"url":"http://seclists.org/fulldisclosure/2010/Aug/84","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_FULLDISC"],"name":"20100807 openssl-1.0.0a"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2010/2229","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2010-2229"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/eng